Subject: [PATCH] Fix compound-score coral-trend wording, WDPA ratio naming,
 and population-weighted disclosure gap
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Round-2 external review caught two real labeling mismatches and one
under-disclosed caveat, none of which involved a data or number change:

- Compound Vulnerability Score's coral input has always been the
  early-vs-recent-period DHW change (coral_dhw_increase), not the
  seasonal Mann-Kendall trend-test result (a separate robustness check,
  Section 4.3). The prose across the paper, README, Executive Summary,
  four dashboard pages, and two chart-generation scripts called it a
  'coral thermal-stress trend' anyway. Renamed to 'coral thermal-stress
  change' everywhere it describes the compound score's actual input,
  and added an explicit distinction from the trend test at first use.

- The WDPA governance ratio (protected area within a 10km coastal
  buffer / island land area) can exceed 1.0 because its numerator can
  include marine protected area near the coast (Seychelles = 11.32).
  Naming it 'Coastal WDPA Protection Ratio' / 'protected-area coverage'
  reads like a land-coverage percentage, which it isn't. Renamed to
  'WDPA Coastal-Buffer Ratio' throughout (paper, README, dashboard axis
  label, static Figure 6), with an explicit definition and the
  exceeds-1.0 explanation added at first use.

- Population-weighted exposure figures are still the v4 bbox-only run;
  the v5 boundary-polygon-mask code exists but hasn't been rerun
  against the real rasters (not in this checkout). This was already
  disclosed in the paper's Limitations and the Executive Summary's
  checklist, but README's robustness-checks paragraph presented it
  caveat-free. Fixed README's wording, moved the hardcoded population
  percentages in research_paper_figures.py into a new
  data/population_weighted_exposure_summary.csv (tagged
  bbox_v4_pending_polygon_mask_rerun) instead of a bare dict, corrected
  a code comment that wrongly claimed a 'validated final run', and
  added the pending-rerun caveat directly to Figure 3's caption image.

Regenerated all affected static figures, interactive plots, and PDFs
(paper/executive-summary/dev-log, root + dashboard/static copies).
Added Dev Log Entry 10 documenting this round. No CSV values, p-values,
scores, or ratios changed — this is entirely a labeling/disclosure fix.

